 {"id":"S001-TEV-MTF-011","gelenek":"tevrat","tur":"motif","ayet":"1:5","islev":"sinir","iliski":"tematik","durum":"acik","kat":"ek","metin":"Levililer 25:42, Mısır'dan çıkarılan İsraillileri Allah'ın kulları saydığı için köle gibi satılmalarını yasaklar: {he:כִּֽי־עֲבָדַ֣י הֵ֔ם, tr:ki avadai hem, gloss:çünkü onlar benim kullarımdır, source:WLC:Lev.25.42}. Ancak 25:46 yabancı kölelerin miras bırakılmasına izin verir. Tesniye 5:14 köleye sahibi gibi Şabat dinlenmesi tanır; Eyüp 31:15 efendiyle hizmetkârın aynı yaratıcıdan geldiğini söyler. Metinlerin insan efendiliğine koyduğu sınırlar kendi içinde de farklıdır.","kaynak":"WLC:Lev.25.42|WLC:Lev.25.46|WLC:Deut.5.14|WLC:Job.31.13|WLC:Job.31.15","paragraf":14,"capa":"Kitap ehline yapılan çağrı ise insanlar arasındaki bu efendilik ilişkisini sınırlar","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"masoretik"}
-{"id":"S001-INC-KRA-002","gelenek":"incil","tur":"karsi_anlati","ayet":"1:5","islev":"karsit","iliski":"karsilastirmali","durum":"acik","kat":"temel","metin":"Filipililer 2:6-11'de Tanrı suretindeki Mesih {el:μορφὴν δούλου λαβών, tr:morphen doulou labon, gloss:kul suretini alarak, source:SBLGNT:Phil.2.7} kendini alçaltır; ardından Allah onu yüceltir ve herkes İsa'yı Rab diye anar. Bu Hristiyan ilahisi, şerhin 'sahip alçalmaz' çizgisinin karşısına yüceliğin hizmet ve alçalma içinden geçtiği başka bir düzen koyar.","kaynak":"SBLGNT:Phil.2.6|SBLGNT:Phil.2.7|SBLGNT:Phil.2.8|SBLGNT:Phil.2.9|SBLGNT:Phil.2.10|SBLGNT:Phil.2.11","paragraf":14,"capa":"Sahip hiçbir şekilde alçalmaz","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"yunanca_ahit"}
-{"id":"S001-INC-KRA-003","gelenek":"incil","tur":"karsi_anlati","ayet":"1:5","islev":"karsit","iliski":"karsilastirmali","durum":"acik","kat":"ek","metin":"Yuhanna 13:13-14'te İsa kendisine 'Rab ve Öğretmen' denmesini kabul ettikten sonra öğrencilerinin ayaklarını yıkadığını söyler: {el:ἔνιψα ὑμῶν τοὺς πόδας, tr:enipsa humon tous podas, gloss:ayaklarınızı yıkadım, source:SBLGNT:John.13.14}. Luka 12:37'de beklenen efendi gelip hizmetkârlarını sofraya oturtur ve onlara hizmet eder. Bu sahnelerde efendi konumu hizmet etmeyi dışlamaz; şerhteki mutlak ayrımdan farklı bir değer örgüsü kurulur.","kaynak":"SBLGNT:John.13.13|SBLGNT:John.13.14|SBLGNT:Luke.12.37","paragraf":14,"capa":"Sahip hiçbir şekilde alçalmaz","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"yunanca_ahit"}
+{"id":"S001-INC-KRA-002","gelenek":"incil","tur":"karsi_anlati","ayet":"1:5","islev":"karsit","iliski":"karsilastirmali","durum":"acik","kat":"temel","metin":"Filipililer 2:6-11'de Tanrı suretindeki Mesih {el:μορφὴν δούλου λαβών, tr:morphen doulou labon, gloss:kul suretini alarak, source:SBLGNT:Phil.2.7} kendini alçaltır; Allah onu yüceltir ve herkes İsa'yı Rab diye anar. Yuhanna 13:13-14'te Rab diye anılan İsa öğrencilerin ayaklarını yıkar; Luka 12:37'de efendi hizmetkârlarına sofra kurar. Bu Hristiyan sahneleri, yücelik ve hizmetin şerhteki katı ayrımdan farklı ilişkisini kurar.","kaynak":"SBLGNT:Phil.2.6|SBLGNT:Phil.2.7|SBLGNT:Phil.2.8|SBLGNT:Phil.2.9|SBLGNT:Phil.2.10|SBLGNT:Phil.2.11|SBLGNT:John.13.13|SBLGNT:John.13.14|SBLGNT:Luke.12.37","paragraf":14,"capa":"Sahip hiçbir şekilde alçalmaz","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"yunanca_ahit"}
+{"id":"S001-INC-KRA-003","gelenek":"incil","tur":"karsi_anlati","ayet":"1:5","islev":"sinir","iliski":"karsilastirmali","durum":"acik","kat":"ek","metin":"Koloseliler 4:1, insan efendilere kölelerine adalet ve eşitlik sağlamalarını, çünkü kendilerinin de gökte bir Rabbi olduğunu söyler: {el:καὶ ὑμεῖς ἔχετε κύριον ἐν ⸀οὐρανῷ, tr:kai hymeis ekhete kyrion en ourano, gloss:sizin de gökte bir Rabbiniz var, source:SBLGNT:Col.4.1}. Efesliler 6:9 tehdidi yasaklar; Filimon 16 kölenin sevgili kardeş olarak kabulünü ister. İlahi efendilik bu metinlerde insan efendinin davranışına sınır getirir.","kaynak":"SBLGNT:Col.4.1|SBLGNT:Eph.6.9|SBLGNT:Phlm.1.16","paragraf":14,"capa":"Kitap ehline yapılan çağrı ise insanlar arasındaki bu efendilik ilişkisini sınırlar","bag":"benzerlik","tarihleme":"kuran_oncesi","nusha":"yunanca_ahit"}

payload.input:
text(await tools.apply_patch("*** Begin Patch
*** Add File: /Volumes/aro/projects/prose_generation/enrichment/bible/work/s001/ehlikitap-images.sol.max.session-20261005/sec2/verdicts.jsonl
+{"connection_id":"BC-6ecddea6766ccd3e72de","ref":"Augustine, City of God 19.15","status":"unavailable","reason":"The patristic passage has no locator in the frozen local snapshot; its proposed natural-rule/slavery distinction cannot be checked here.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-38907a1b1650c9abce52","ref":"Augustine, Confessions 1.1.1","status":"unavailable","reason":"The Confessions passage has no local witness in this run, so the creation-and-rest reading remains unverified.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f8d95fd9ea607d8af973","ref":"Didache 4:10","status":"unavailable","reason":"No Didache text was imported into the local snapshot; the quoted household instruction cannot be verified.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-6458cf9bb2801c7cc78b","ref":"Gregory of Nyssa, Homilies on Ecclesiastes 4","status":"unavailable","reason":"This homily lacks a local locator, so its critique of human purchase cannot be checked against a witness.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c334e7ef6d3847c7f101","ref":"Ignatius, To Polycarp 4:3","status":"unavailable","reason":"The Ignatius letter is absent from this local snapshot; the proposed counsel to slaves is unverified.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d7a6542ba9d5a47d68c4","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.6.19","status":"accepted","reason":"Paul explicitly denies believers' self-ownership; the next verse supplies the purchase rationale used in paragraph 10.","paragraphs":[10],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.6.19","SBLGNT:1Cor.6.20"],"annotations":["S001-INC-MTF-004"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-dd26af35e48a52c4c027","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.6.20","status":"accepted","reason":"The Greek says believers were bought for a price and should glorify God bodily, completing the ownership motif.","paragraphs":[10],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.6.19","SBLGNT:1Cor.6.20"],"annotations":["S001-INC-MTF-004"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-ca87099b0e81f5f85c28","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.7.22","status":"accepted","reason":"The free called person is called Christ's slave; the paired enslaved person's freedom qualifies social status.","paragraphs":[13],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.2.16","SBLGNT:1Cor.7.22","SBLGNT:1Cor.7.23","SBLGNT:Rom.6.22"],"annotations":["S001-INC-MTF-011"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-56c0e1d60b321b5cdfdb","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.7.22","status":"accepted","reason":"The verse explicitly pairs a Lord's freedperson with a free person enslaved to Christ; it is a revaluation of social labels, not their abolition.","paragraphs":[13],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.2.16","SBLGNT:1Cor.7.22","SBLGNT:1Cor.7.23","SBLGNT:Rom.6.22"],"annotations":["S001-INC-MTF-011"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-7a0bf288d067728348c4","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.7.23","status":"accepted","reason":"The command not to become human slaves follows the divine purchase statement and limits rival human claims.","paragraphs":[13],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.2.16","SBLGNT:1Cor.7.22","SBLGNT:1Cor.7.23","SBLGNT:Rom.6.22"],"annotations":["S001-INC-MTF-011"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-55e7df3dc6ba0ca4c8ab","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.7.23","status":"accepted","reason":"The contrast between being bought and becoming human slaves is explicit, though the text is a command within Paul's argument, not a legal ban on all slavery.","paragraphs":[13],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.2.16","SBLGNT:1Cor.7.22","SBLGNT:1Cor.7.23","SBLGNT:Rom.6.22"],"annotations":["S001-INC-MTF-011"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-2ab5332a13e5140bb029","ref":"SBLGNT:1Cor.9.19","status":"rejected","reason":"Paul voluntarily makes himself a servant to all for mission; the paragraph concerns prior divine belonging by creation, so this is a different kind of service.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Cor.9.19"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-29be2ab7b43b18be1d20","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.2.16","status":"accepted","reason":"The verse explicitly orders free people to live as God's slaves, preserving both terms together.","paragraphs":[13],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.2.16","SBLGNT:1Cor.7.22","SBLGNT:1Cor.7.23","SBLGNT:Rom.6.22"],"annotations":["S001-INC-MTF-011"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-3ef7b2e652b1180ca8b3","ref":"SBLGNT:1Pet.2.16","status":"accepted","reason":"The freedom/divine-slavery juxtaposition is explicit; it reframes rather than denies the claim of belonging.","paragraphs":[13],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Pet.2.16","SBLGNT:1Cor.7.22","SBLGNT:1Cor.7.23","SBLGNT:Rom.6.22"],"annotations":["S001-INC-MTF-011"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-f77696b89c7b9b4f63ba","ref":"SBLGNT:1Tim.6.1","status":"rejected","reason":"The instruction concerns social honor for human masters, not worship of them; it cannot substantiate the B006 worship-like honor gloss.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Tim.6.1"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-3ac22fa9dc0a248cb55b","ref":"SBLGNT:1Tim.6.15","status":"rejected","reason":"The royal doxology is genuine but supplies no household ownership or servitude detail beyond the more precise royal and judicial passages selected for paragraphs 10–11.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["SBLGNT:1Tim.6.15"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-4317c652e9b1345a33e9","ref":"SBLGNT:2Cor.5.10","status":"rejected","reason":"This is specifically Christ's tribunal and individual recompense; Revelation 14:7 more directly joins the creator, worship and judgment hour at paragraph 11.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Cor.5.10"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-2c26a0410fedac2919d5","ref":"SBLGNT:2Cor.5.10","status":"rejected","reason":"The individual accounting is real, but it repeats the judgment-seat point without the master/slave relation or the day itself.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["SBLGNT:2Cor.5.10"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-0ba1962b7931a9817154","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.10.25","status":"rejected","reason":"Cornelius prostrates before Peter, but this verse alone says neither that Peter is a lord nor that the act is worship; the refusal comes in 10:26 and is not a household-master parallel.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.10.25"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-c35a2e6f06834c7ca7ae","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.10.26","status":"rejected","reason":"Peter's refusal is explicit but addresses prostration to an apostle, a cultic boundary distinct from paragraph 14's human-owner relation.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.10.26"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-beb0083bb12acc8af2a3","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.14.15","status":"rejected","reason":"The apostles redirect worship toward the creator, but the verse contains no master or owned-person relation; Matthew 4:10 carries the exclusive worship point more directly.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.14.15"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-d540a1a8151b0462d44d","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.17.24","status":"accepted","reason":"The Greek explicitly calls the world's maker Lord of heaven and earth; its continuation denies need for human service.","paragraphs":[10],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.4.24","SBLGNT:Acts.17.24","SBLGNT:Acts.17.25"],"annotations":["S001-INC-MTF-003"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-30bc9e73738832416e35","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.17.25","status":"accepted","reason":"The creator gives life and needs no human-hand attendance, qualifying the household servant analogy.","paragraphs":[10],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.4.24","SBLGNT:Acts.17.24","SBLGNT:Acts.17.25"],"annotations":["S001-INC-MTF-003"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-27d97531a863a21b2303","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.17.25","status":"accepted","reason":"The explicit absence of divine need supports the distinction between service to God and supplying a needy human owner.","paragraphs":[10],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.4.24","SBLGNT:Acts.17.24","SBLGNT:Acts.17.25"],"annotations":["S001-INC-MTF-003"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-0cd293de689270c8be0e","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.17.31","status":"accepted","reason":"The verse explicitly speaks of an appointed day to judge the inhabited world, supporting the day-of-judgment dimension.","paragraphs":[11],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Rev.14.7","SBLGNT:Acts.17.31","SBLGNT:Rev.20.12"],"annotations":["S001-INC-MTF-007"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-6b885e462bb9f17fa1de","ref":"SBLGNT:Acts.4.24","status":"accepted","reason":"The prayer directly addresses the maker of heaven and earth as despotes, joining address, creation and mastery.","paragraphs":[10],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Acts.4.24","SBLGNT:Acts.17.24","SBLGNT:Acts.17.25"],"annotations":["S001-INC-MTF-003"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-b25f892bc814299c9ca0","ref":"SBLGNT:Col.3.24","status":"rejected","reason":"The verse tells household slaves to serve Christ for an inheritance; it does not state the reciprocal limit on their human masters articulated in Colossians 4:1.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.3.24"],"annotations":[]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-85d111ecbcd2583c596d","ref":"SBLGNT:Col.4.1","status":"accepted","reason":"The command to earthly masters cites their own heavenly Lord and directly constrains household power.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.4.1","SBLGNT:Eph.6.9","SBLGNT:Phlm.1.16"],"annotations":["S001-INC-KRA-003"]}
+{"connection_id":"BC-2168821f8a50f4f4c909","ref":"SBLGNT:Eph.6.9","status":"accepted","reason":"The shared heavenly Lord and prohibition of threats explicitly constrain human masters.","paragraphs":[14],"evidence":["SBLGNT:Col.4.1","SBLGNT:Eph.6.9","SBLGNT:Phlm.1.16"],"annotations":["S001-INC-KRA-003"]}
