{"connection_id":"BC-0f0cc6f8ca5e1aaf027a","ref":"WLC:Ps.95.7","status":"rejected","reason":"The flock-of-hand line concerns shepherd care rather than an owned human slave; Psalm 100:3 supplies the comparable flock image alongside making.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Ps.95.7"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-b84509352e08dbdc4b4c","ref":"WLC:Zech.14.9","status":"accepted","reason":"The inflected Hebrew le-melekh names YHWH king of all the earth; the root match does not prove the Arabic property nuance.","paragraphs":[10],"evidence":["WLC:Zech.14.9","WLC:Isa.6.5"],"annotations":["S001-TEV-SYD-001"]}
{"connection_id":"BC-56d9f6033e261c8ed1e5","ref":"WLC:Zech.9.9","status":"rejected","reason":"Zion's humble king rides an ass, but he is a human royal entrant, not the divine owner of a servant; Matthew 21:5 repeats this scene.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Zech.9.9"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":"BC-42a2984e5bb84b02e665","ref":"Wisdom of Solomon 16:24","status":"unavailable","reason":"Wisdom 16:24 has no imported original text in this run; creation-serves-maker wording cannot be verified.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":[],"annotations":[]}
