{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"WLC:Deut.15.12","status":"rejected","reason":"It states release in the seventh year, but Exodus 21:2 states the same term in the selected legal-limits note and Leviticus 25:42 gives its theological rationale.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.15.12"],"annotations":[]}
{"connection_id":null,"origin":"research","ref":"WLC:Deut.15.13","status":"rejected","reason":"It says the released Hebrew servant must not leave empty handed; this is provision on release, not a new owner-status or worship claim in the image.","paragraphs":[],"evidence":["WLC:Deut.15.13"],"annotations":[]}
